 "notes": "Continuation of Table XV Part II(B) Tri and poly-lingualism. Subsidiary column headers on header pages of this part print 'Dogri.', 'Panjabi.', 'Kashmiri.' (leaf 266 adds letters (B),(C),(D)); recorded as Dogri/Panjabi/Kashmiri. Rows printed nil ('....') in every column are omitted; subsidiary triples all-nil are omitted. Remarks: wrapped lines joined; a word broken across lines ('langu-'/'ages.' or 'langu'/'ages.') is rejoined as 'languages.'. Page 261. Top rows (Gojari..Shina) continue the Srinagar Municipality block of Kashmir South from leaf 270 (brace label 'Srinagar Municipality' and 'Kashmir South.' printed on this page). Kashmir North (printed 'Kashmir North.', 'N' damaged) tehsils: Sri Pratapsinghpura, Baramulla, Uttarmachhipura (block continues on leaf 272 with Panjabi..Shina). Rows all-nil omitted: Srinagar Chabhali, Pothwari; Sri Pratapsinghpura Chabhali, Pothwari; Baramulla Gojari, Chabhali, Pothwari, Ladakhi. Srinagar Balti remark printed '3 langu' / 'ages.' with no hyphen; Uttarmachhipura Gojari and Western Pahari remarks hyphenated 'langu-'/'ages.'. Printed spelling 'Uttarmachhipura Tehsil' (second line looks like 'Teheil' in bold italic, read as Tehsil)."
}